The source changes appear build-integrated, but the patch violates the project correctness gate by marking stmap5 validated without adding the required canonical version-log entry.

Review comment:

- [P2] Record stmap5 before marking it validated — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json:55-55
  When this state marks `stmap5` as evaluated/validated, the AutoEDA contract requires every successful numbered version to append a `## versionN` entry to `.autoeda/runtime/versions.md` with hypothesis, validation, benchmark results, review outcome, and next-step recommendation. This patch adds and evaluates `stmap5`, but `versions.md` still ends at version4, so the iteration cannot be counted or audited from the canonical campaign log.
